// The fourteen magic tablets the lecterns make.
//
// GENERATED by tools/gentablets.py from tools/tabletspec.json. Edit the generator.
//
// All fourteen are obj_zarosstonetablet, the one tablet-shaped inventory model 377 has, under two
// recolour pairs. That model carries exactly two face colours - 28 faces of 12651 for the slab and
// 14 of 9480 for the marks cut into it (tools/models/ob2palette.py) - so recolouring both turns the
// whole tablet without touching the geometry. recolNs/recolNd are RGB555, five bits a channel; the
// packer converts to the model's HSL16 at pack time. See claude/obj-recolours.md.
//
// The 2d camera is the Zaros tablet's own, which is what makes the icon read as a slab rather than
// a pebble. iop1=Break is on the ones that do something by themselves; the five enchant tablets
// have no iop1 because an enchant needs a target - you use them on the ring or amulet.

